            <ArticleTitle>Hematoma of the rectus abdominis muscle: case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>165-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hematoma of the rectus abdominis muscle, although a well-described clinical entity, is commonly misdiagnosed. A case of abdominal pain associated with the subjective perception of a &quot;lump,&quot; which proved to be a rectus abdominis hematoma, is presented. The pathoanatomy, presenting symptoms, investigation, and treatment options for the condition are reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
